  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday) \nIssued at 322 AM EDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nFor the first part of next week we return to a pattern consisting of \nridging aloft and moderate easterly flow around the base of a low-\nlevel ridge. That means a return to scattered passing showers each \nday and night. The pattern will change a bit come mid-week when flow \nbegins to veer ahead of a developing/approaching frontal system. \nThere's still quite a bit of uncertainty around the pre-frontal \nenvironment and how mesoscale features will affect storm \ndistribution each day, but guidance is in fair agreement of a \nfrontal passage some time on Friday. How strong and how far south \nthe surface low will be, and what that means for the potential for \nan isolated severe storm or two, remains in question with quite a \nbit of model spread. Certainly something to keep an eye on once we \nget past this weekends heavy rain threat.",
